(:adr
  :id "D84"
  :shortcode "D84"
  :title "Multi-Client Launcher Engine, Dangerous-Rescue Permissions, and Client Channel Protocol"
  :status :active
  :planStatus :approved
  :date "2026-09-13"
  :cluster "architecture/launcher"
  :deciders ["user" "architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "Autonomous agents running across heterogeneous client environments (Antigravity CLI, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf) face fractured startup flags, fragile environment injection, manual permission prompts that stall autonomous workflows, and missing native binary aliases (addie, eddie). Specifically, Antigravity requires automatic injection of --dangerously-skip-permissions under permission-tier dangerous-rescue and channel binding to RULE user_global, while Claude Code path discovery fails when installed in user-local directories rather than global paths."
  :drivers [
    "Unified Startup Interface: Single command surface (asl launch <client>) abstracting per-client CLI flags, environment variables, and sandbox boundaries."
    "Automated Dangerous-Rescue Permission Elevation: Unattended autonomous sessions automatically configure permission tiers without interactive prompt deadlock."
    "Deterministic Multi-Client Discovery: Priority-ordered resolution across local directories (~/.local/bin, ~/bin), application bundles, and PATH."
    "Native Wrapper Scaffolding: Automated generation and maintenance of bin/addie and bin/eddie client wrappers bound to bin/asl."
    "Structured Channel Protocol Handshake: Transparent launch-session handshake validating active rules, permission tier, and measured capability lock."
  ]
  :evidence [
    "User directive explicitly demanded fixing agy launcher with --dangerously-skip-permissions and resolving other client execution issues."
    "Interactive permission prompts in unattended subagent sessions halt autonomous progress indefinitely."
    "Hardcoded /usr/local/bin paths fail on Apple Silicon systems using /opt/homebrew or ~/.local/bin."
    "ADR D43 and D80 establish client channel boundaries and workspace lineage visibility."
  ]
  :decision "Adopt D84 establishing the canonical Multi-Client Launcher Engine in asl/tools/asl.c and asl/grammar/launch.asn. Implement structured permission tiering (read-only, sandboxed-write, dangerous-rescue), deterministic client path discovery with user-local overrides, native binary scaffolding for addie and eddie, and dry-run capability handshakes via asl launch --dry-run."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D81" "D84"]
  :tasks [
    "Task48501"
    "Task48502"
    "Task48503"
    "Task48504"
    "Task48505"
    "Task48506"
  ]
  :settledChoices [
    (:choice :id launcherInterface :value "Native CLI subcommand asl launch <client> [args]")
    (:choice :id agyFlags :value "Automatic injection of --dangerously-skip-permissions when permission-tier is dangerous-rescue")
    (:choice :id claudeDiscovery :value "Priority resolution: ~/.local/bin/claude before system PATH")
    (:choice :id nativeAliases :value "Scaffold bin/addie and bin/eddie shell shims delegating to bin/asl with client context")
    (:choice :id dryRunOutput :value "Dense ASN receipt reporting resolved binary path, flags, permission tier, and channel status")
  ]
  :outcomes [
    "Zero interactive permission stalls during autonomous Antigravity and Claude execution runs"
    "Robust client resolution across macOS Apple Silicon, Intel, and Linux development environments"
    "First-class addie and eddie binary wrappers operating in harmony with bin/asl"
    "Structured launch-session handshakes recorded in session ledgers for epistemic auditability"
  ]
)
